### ManualMate — manual endpoint tests (run in Rider / VS / VS Code REST Client)
### Make sure the API is running: dotnet run --launch-profile http  (http://localhost:5035)

@host = http://localhost:5035
### Put a real item id here after creating one — or use the ready-to-go LG Microwave item
### (already processed & askable, left in the DB after the Nov 14 setup)
@itemId = 071d39f2-5a14-4361-92bc-7bddc6ee7b4a

### 1. List items (after startup there should be exactly 1 seeded item: Samsung Galaxy S24)
GET {{host}}/api/item

### 2. Get one item (use a real id from the list above)
GET {{host}}/api/item/{{itemId}}

### 3. Create item + upload manual  → triggers async processing (RabbitMQ)
###    Watch logs/ or the DB: Status goes Pending → Processing → Completed
POST {{host}}/api/item
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

LG Microwave
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

A microwave oven is a kitchen appliance that heats and cooks food by exposing it to electromagnetic radiation in the microwave frequency range
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="LG_Microwave.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./wwwroot/Files/LG_Microwave.pdf
--WebAppBoundary--

### 4. Ask a question (works right away on the LG Microwave item — already Completed)
GET {{host}}/api/item/ask/{{itemId}}?question=How do I set the clock?
### Ask again → served from Redis cache (much faster the 2nd time)

### 5. Edit item (name/description only; no file → just omit it)
PUT {{host}}/api/item/{{itemId}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

LG Microwave Oven
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Updated description for testing the PUT endpoint
--WebAppBoundary--

### 6. Replace the manual file of an existing item (restored endpoint)
###    NOTE: replaces the file only — embeddings are NOT regenerated (see guide)
POST {{host}}/api/item/upload-manual/{{itemId}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="DualSense.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./wwwroot/Files/DualSense_d0e5f9ced79b49c7acf9c6ced1daba01.pdf
--WebAppBoundary--

### 7. Delete item (also deletes its embeddings; the PDF file stays on disk)
DELETE {{host}}/api/item/{{itemId}}

### ---------- Edge cases ----------

### 8. Non-existing item → 404
GET {{host}}/api/item/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 9. Create without file → 400 (validation: "File is required")
POST {{host}}/api/item
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

No File Item
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

This request has no file on purpose
--WebAppBoundary--

### 10. Create with wrong file type → 400 ("File type .txt is not allowed")
POST {{host}}/api/item
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

Wrong Type
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Uploading a text file on purpose
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="notes.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

< ./appsettings.json
--WebAppBoundary--

### 11. Oversized file (> 50 MB) → 400 from the app's own validation
###     (Kestrel limit was raised to 60 MB so the app-level check is reachable)
POST {{host}}/api/item
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WebAppBoundary

--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="name"

Too Big
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

dell service manual is ~52 MB on purpose
--WebAppBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="dell-g15-5520-service-manual-en-us.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./wwwroot/Files/dell-g15-5520-service-manual-en-us.pdf
--WebAppBoundary--

### 12. Ask on a not-yet-processed item → 400 "is not processed yet"
GET {{host}}/api/item/ask/{{itemId}}?question=anything

### 13. Swagger UI
GET {{host}}/swagger/index.html
